      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The use of a prior density that conjugates the likelihood allows us to develop analytic expressions of the posterior density. As we will see in Appendix 3, this is critical in developing Gibbs samplers for problems of interest. Table A2.2 summarizes the conjugate priors for several common likelihood functions, with the various families of distributions discussed below.",
